\mathrm{CHO}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_3-\\mathrm{CHO}$ and $\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO}$","$\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO}$ and HCHO","All of the above"],"answer":2,"solution":"Cannizaro reaction is possible in which aldehyde where the $\\alpha$-hydrogen atoms are absent.\ne.g. $\\mathrm{HCHO}, \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO}2 \\mathrm{HCHO}-\\xrightarrow[\\Delta]{\\mathrm{NaOH}} \\mathrm{HCOONa}+\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{OH}\\begin{aligned}\n2 \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO}-\\stackrel{\\mathrm{NaOH}}{\\Delta} & \\mathrm{C}_6 \\\\\n\\mathrm{H}_5 & \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH} \\\\\n& +\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{COONa}\n\\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2019","_marksId":"67921e561d5b5072da5ea23a"},{"id":52600,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Aldehydes and Ketones","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"In the Cannizzaro reaction given below\n$2 \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}} \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{COO}^{-}$\nThe slowest step is","options":["The attack of $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$ at the carbonyl group","The transfer of hydride ion to the carbonyl aroun","The abstraction of proton from the carboxylic acid","The deprotonation of benzyl alcohol"],"answer":1,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fmanipal%252F_sA-MWB4h-cnhIHlaeIv9XyJ1tk7oKIxrwZaGU-KWmU.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmanipal%2F_sA-MWB4h-cnhIHlaeIv9XyJ1tk7oKIxrwZaGU-KWmU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmanipal%2F_sA-MWB4h-cnhIHlaeIv9XyJ1tk7oKIxrwZaGU-KWmU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>$\\mathrmH^{-}$ is obtained by fission of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond of $(\\mathrm{B})$. It is transferred to (II). This is the slowest step.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2020","_marksId":"67921e671d5b5072da5ea2bf"},{"id":52601,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Aldehydes and Ketones","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Which of the following pairs give positive Tollen's test?","options":["Glucose, sucrose","Glucose, fractose","Hexanal, acetophenone","Fractose, sucrose"],"answer":1,"solution":"Aldehyde and $\\alpha$-hydroxy ketones give positive Tollen's test. Glucose has an aldehyde group and fructose is an $\\alpha$-hydroxy ketone.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"Manipal (MET) 2015","_marksId":"67921dff1d5b5072da5e9f86"},{"id":52602,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Aldehydes and Ketones","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Which of the following statements is not true for acetaldehyde?","options":["It will undergo an aldol condensation reaction.","It will undergo a Cannizzaro reaction.","It will undergo a haloform reaction","Enolisation ic catalysed by acid or base"],"answer":1,"solution":"Acetaldehyde contains $\\alpha-\\mathrm{H}$, so it undergoes aldol condensation rather than Cannizzaro reaction.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2014","_marksId":"67921de51d5b5072da5e9ec4"},{"id":52603,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Aldehydes and Ketones","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Based on the following reaction identify alkene\n$\\mathrm{A} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{O}_3 /\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right) / \\mathrm{Zn}} 2 \\mathrm{HCHO}+\\underset{\\mathrm{CHO}}{\\mathrm{CHO}}$","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fmanipal%252F3bU7N8U8t9Ft-TcDIbo